  "note": "Self-written insurance claim forms and settlement statements (保険金請求書・保険金支払明細 / insurance claim form, settlement statement) for made-up insurers and made-up claimants, with fictional amounts and fictional policy numbers: a hospital benefit claim and a car damage claim settlement, each in a clean version and a planted one that differs only on the lines below. The insurance set covers product summaries; this set covers claims and payouts. They run as business/proposal, the genre the medical bills and payslips run as: no genre is made for insurance claims. Each mistake names its kind, the line it is on, the text the clean line has there (clean) and the planted line has instead (planted), and the rule expected to report it on that line; a mistake that breaks a pair of lines names the pair's other line as pairedLine. The days in hospital times the daily benefit is named for line-amount-mismatch, and the plant changes the daily benefit, not the amount, so the benefits still add up to the total; the daily benefit is written nowhere else. The covered amount minus the deductible is named for net-amount-mismatch, and the plant changes the amount paid, which no sentence repeats. A claim date before the date of the incident and a discharge date before the admission date are named for due-before-issue, which compares a pair of labelled dates on their own lines. The days in hospital stated in the table and again in a sentence of the same section is named for fact-conflict. The policy number written with two neighbouring digits swapped is named for reference-number-variant, and the claimant's name written two ways for name-variant. Each plant was also run alone on its clean document, so no plant depends on another. yarn planted claims scores them; expected.json is the committed score.",
